{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":30000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-sol","packSha":"1c4ecdd5b741899a3d292f2e6ccf4917984d763788e6abfd50dc5dd90d97841f","packTokens":11616,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":2,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":196,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"intent","tokens":331,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":672,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"assumptions","tokens":1,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"cb","tokens":1638,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"spec","tokens":8688,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":5,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"critic"},"pointers":[],"system":"Adversarial reviewer. Find defects in this spec; don't praise; don't rewrite it.\nRubric: 1 conflicts between requirements 2 missing error, empty and permission paths 3 ACs not observable at a public surface 4 scope creep beyond the intent 5 claims about existing behaviour without anchors 6 state transitions and existing data 7 behaviour changes outside the requested scope (blast radius) 8 hardcoded identifiers that should be configuration.\nEach finding: rubric number, reqId, severity (critical|high|medium|low), one-sentence evidence in \"finding\". Empty list if none.\nThe human answered questions and accepted assumptions (below). Scope they decided is not a defect: don't flag it.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"intent\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"changeClass\": \"feature\",\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-13T17:39:00.587Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"intent\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n   \"stage\": \"intake\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20261013-hackathon-problem-statement-fe-2bf7\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"rigor\": \"full\",\n \"risk\": \"medium\",\n \"riskTags\": [\n  \"public-api\",\n  \"migration\"\n ],\n \"source\": \"cli\",\n \"spans\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-1\",\n   \"text\": \"Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-2\",\n   \"text\": \"Keep the data in the project's PostgreSQL database (the connection string named App, which the project already reads).\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-3\",\n   \"text\": \"Write sample data in App.Api/SeedData.cs: a few believable rows for each table, taken from the contract's examples, so each list has something to show.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-4\",\n   \"text\": \"No test may count on those rows, because the app runs that file only when the setting Seed:Demo is true.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"I-5\",\n   \"text\": \"Do not build screens here; the web app is built in its own repo.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"touchesUi\": false\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Should authentication and authorization be enforced only where contracts/openapi.yaml explicitly requires them, or should additional access rules be added?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Enforce only authentication/authorization requirements explicitly declared by contracts/openapi.yaml; do not add extra role rules.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen for paths or HTTP methods that are not defined in the contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use normal 404/405 responses and add no undocumented operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"If demo seed data cannot be written to PostgreSQL when Seed:Demo is true, how should startup behave?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail startup and surface the seed-write error.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Should successful API writes remain available after the API process restarts?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use normal PostgreSQL durability so successful writes remain available after an API restart.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Should all 13 requirements be approved as one run, or should the work be split by cutting or deferring a part?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Approve all 13 requirements in one run.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Should lot-list responses apply an additional authorizedYards restriction beyond the filtering and security rules declared in the API contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply only the lot-list filtering and security rules declared in contracts/openapi.yaml; add no authorizedYards restriction.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the profitability permission checks be covered for users with view and export permissions independently?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Add separate cases for the contract-defined view-only and export-only paths, checking their respective redaction and export-denial behavior.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"After correcting or voiding a feeding event, how should the resulting stock be calculated when other persisted movements affect the same items?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Calculate stock using opening stock and all persisted receipts, adjustments, and feeding events, incorporating the correction or void.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"assumptions\" kind=\"assumptions\" sha=\"\">\n[]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"cb\" kind=\"current-behaviour\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"claims\": [\n  {\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 14,\n     \"lineStart\": 11,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"  /auth/sign-in:\\n    post:\\n      operationId: signIn\\n      summary: \\\"Sign in with email and password.\\\"\",\n     \"symbol\": \"paths./auth/sign-in.post\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 31,\n     \"lineStart\": 27,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"app.UseCors();\\napp.MapGet(\\\"/\\\", () => \\\"API is up\\\").ExcludeFromDescription();\\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\\napp.MapOpenApi();\\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\\\"/openapi/v1.json\\\", \\\"API\\\"));\",\n     \"symbol\": \"Program\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"id\": \"C-I1\",\n   \"spans\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"text\": \"The contract defines operations such as POST /auth/sign-in (operationId signIn), but the current app maps only the root health endpoint; it exposes OpenAPI and Swagger UI, not handlers for the contract operations.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 9,\n     \"lineStart\": 8,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"builder.Services.AddDbContext<AppDb>(o => o.UseNpgsql(builder.Configuration.GetConnectionString(\\\"App\\\")\\n    ?? throw new InvalidOperationException(\\\"No database connection is configured. Set ConnectionStrings__App (for example Host=...;Port=5432;Database=...;Username=...;Password=«SECRET_1»\")));\",\n     \"symbol\": \"Program\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 22,\n     \"lineStart\": 20,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"        using var scope = app.Services.CreateScope();\\n        var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<AppDb>();\\n        db.Database.EnsureCreated();\",\n     \"symbol\": \"Program\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 7,\n     \"lineStart\": 5,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/AppDb.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"public class AppDb(DbContextOptions<AppDb> options) : DbContext(options)\\n{\\n}\",\n     \"symbol\": \"AppDb\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"id\": \"C-I2\",\n   \"spans\": [\n    \"I-2\"\n   ],\n   \"text\": \"The app configures EF Core to use PostgreSQL with the connection string named App, and ensures the database is created at startup. The current AppDb context has an empty body, so it does not yet declare application tables or DbSets.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 9,\n     \"lineStart\": 7,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/SeedData.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"    public static void Run(AppDb db)\\n    {\\n    }\",\n     \"symbol\": \"SeedData.Run\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 24,\n     \"lineStart\": 23,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"        // sample rows, only when asked for (Seed__Demo=true): tests and the factory's own checks start on an empty database\\n        if (app.Configuration.GetValue<bool>(\\\"Seed:Demo\\\")) SeedData.Run(db);\",\n     \"symbol\": \"Program\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 170,\n     \"lineStart\": 169,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"                  - id: 701\\n                    vendor: \\\"Prairie Livestock\\\"\",\n     \"symbol\": \"paths./imports/source-records.get.responses.200.content.application/json.example\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"id\": \"C-I3\",\n   \"spans\": [\n    \"I-3\"\n   ],\n   \"text\": \"SeedData.Run currently has an empty body, so no sample rows are inserted. Startup invokes it only when Seed:Demo is true; the contract's example values therefore are not currently loaded as seed data.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 24,\n     \"lineStart\": 23,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"        // sample rows, only when asked for (Seed__Demo=true): tests and the factory's own checks start on an empty database\\n        if (app.Configuration.GetValue<bool>(\\\"Seed:Demo\\\")) SeedData.Run(db);\",\n     \"symbol\": \"Program\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 4,\n     \"lineStart\": 3,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/SeedData.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"// Sample rows for a person trying the product. The app calls Run at startup, after the tables exist, only when the setting\\n// Seed:Demo is true (the factory's run files set it; tests never do). Add rows to a table only when that table is empty.\",\n     \"symbol\": \"SeedData\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 16,\n     \"lineStart\": 13,\n     \"path\": \"App.Tests/HealthTests.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"    public async Task ApiIsUp()\\n    {\\n        var res = await _factory.CreateClient().GetAsync(\\\"/\\\");\\n        Assert.Equal(HttpStatusCode.OK, res.StatusCode);\",\n     \"symbol\": \"HealthTests.ApiIsUp\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"id\": \"C-I4\",\n   \"spans\": [\n    \"I-4\"\n   ],\n   \"text\": \"The seed call is gated on Seed:Demo, and the seed-data comment says tests never set that setting. The current test only requests / and checks for HTTP 200; it does not assert or depend on seeded row counts or contents.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 31,\n     \"lineStart\": 28,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"app.MapGet(\\\"/\\\", () => \\\"API is up\\\").ExcludeFromDescription();\\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\\napp.MapOpenApi();\\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\\\"/openapi/v1.json\\\", \\\"API\\\"));\",\n     \"symbol\": \"Program\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"id\": \"C-I5\",\n   \"spans\": [\n    \"I-5\"\n   ],\n   \"text\": \"The current app exposes an API health endpoint and Swagger's API-reading/testing page; Program does not map feedlot product-screen routes. The UI visible from this app is Swagger, not product screens.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"header\": {\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-13T17:40:55.067Z\",\n  \"inputsHash\": \"\",\n  \"kind\": \"current-behaviour\",\n  \"producedBy\": {\n   \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n   \"stage\": \"ground\"\n  },\n  \"runId\": \"20261013-hackathon-problem-statement-fe-2bf7\",\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1\n },\n \"notFound\": []\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API is running and a client has valid contract inputs and any authentication context required by the contract.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Each response status and response body field matches the operation's declared contract, including success and error responses.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client calls each declared operation using its contract-defined method, path, parameters, and request body.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client calls a protected operation without valid authentication or without contract-required authorization.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is the contract-declared 401 or 403, as applicable, and no undeclared role rule denies an otherwise authorized request.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client calls that operation.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API host is running.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 404 for an undefined path or 405 for an unsupported method, and no feedlot product screen is displayed.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client requests an undefined path such as /yard, or uses an unsupported method for a contract path such as POST /dashboard.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot API shall implement every path, HTTP method, parameter, request and response schema, status code, and security rule declared in contracts/openapi.yaml, expose no undocumented API operations, and provide no feedlot product-screen routes or rendered screens.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-2\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client requests sign-in, session, dashboard, or lot-list operations, the Feedlot API shall return the contract-defined authentication, current-user, dashboard, and filtered lot values.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-6\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A client has valid sign-in credentials and no bearer token.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends POST /auth/sign-in with the contract SignInRequest body.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains the contract-defined accessToken and user fields, including declared permissions and authorizedYards.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /session.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response user field contains the current user and contract-defined permissions.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.3\",\n     \"given\": \"Authorized dashboard data and a valid rankBy value of fcr, adg, or costOfGain are available.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /dashboard with the selected rankBy value.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response rankingMeasure, bestLots, and worstLots correspond to the selected measure.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.4\",\n     \"given\": \"Lots have distinct pen, breed, sex, and status values and the client has a valid bearer token.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /lots with supported query filters.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response lots list contains only rows matching the supplied filters and contract-defined fields.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.5\",\n     \"given\": \"A client has the access required by the contract for GET /lots, and saved lots include a lot outside the client's authorizedYards that matches the supplied lot-list filters.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /lots with those supported query filters.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response lots list includes that matching lot with its contract-defined fields, without an additional authorizedYards restriction.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and the source adapter is available.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response records field is a list of available procurement and receiving records.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /imports/source-records.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and submits a valid ImportRequest selecting source records.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains status, createdCount, updatedCount, records, and allocationConflicts fields reflecting the selected records and current matches.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends POST /imports.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and valid PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen allocation quantities.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Both response statuses are 200 and the response poLines, lotPens, and pens contain the saved quantities, traceability status, and capacity information.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client calls PUT /allocations and then GET /allocations.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client submits an invalid selection, conflicting import, or allocation that violates saved state.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status and error response match the operation's declared 409 or 422 contract.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client submits the relevant import or allocation request.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client previews or imports procurement records or saves allocations, the Feedlot API shall return and persist contract-defined PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen traceability, including import matching and allocation-conflict results.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and the requested lot exists.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains the lot forecast values, forecastBasis, and effective yard and lot assumptions.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /lots/{lotId}/forecast.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and submits a valid ForecastSettingsRequest.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains persisted setting values; a subsequent forecast response contains the effective assumptions and projectedMarketDate declared by the contract.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends PATCH /forecast-settings or PATCH /lots/{lotId}/forecast-settings for an existing lot.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and the requested lot exists with feeding and weight records where applicable.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains contract-defined metrics or suggestions with their basis, including null unavailable metric values where applicable.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /lots/{lotId}/metrics or GET /lots/{lotId}/insights.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token, an existing lot, and a valid planner-selected insight action or WeightMeasurementRequest.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status and response fields match the contract, and the returned action or measurement is present in the subsequent relevant response.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends POST /lots/{lotId}/insights/actions, GET /lots/{lotId}/weights, or POST /lots/{lotId}/weights as applicable.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client submits a weight measurement that fails contract validation, or requests forecast data or settings for a nonexistent lot.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.5\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is the contract-declared 422 with VALIDATION_ERROR for invalid measurement data or 404 with NOT_FOUND for a nonexistent lot.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends the applicable weight, forecast, or forecast-settings request.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client requests lot forecasts, forecast-setting updates, metrics, insights, planner actions, or weight-history operations, the Feedlot API shall return contract-defined values, calculations, explainable suggestions, and persisted updates.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and inventory items or movements exist, or the inventory is empty.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains operationalTotals, items, movements, and contract-defined stock fields.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /inventory.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and submits a valid InventoryItemRequest for creation or update.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 201 for creation or 200 for update and the response item contains the saved contract fields and stock values.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends POST /inventory/items or PATCH /inventory/items/{itemId}.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and submits a valid receipt or adjustment InventoryMovementRequest for an existing item.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the response contains the saved movement and item with updated stock values.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends POST /inventory/movements.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token, a supported horizon, and inventory with applicable plans and wastage settings.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Each response status is 200 and each response contains the selected horizon, projection rows with projected consumption and balance, and movement distinctions.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /inventory/projections separately for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, semiAnnual, and annual horizons.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and submits an inventory request that fails contract validation or a projection horizon outside the contract enum.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.5\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 422 and the response error code is VALIDATION_ERROR.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends the applicable inventory write or projection request.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and authorized operational inventory rows exist.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.6\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains fileName, contentType text/csv, and a Base64 CSV file derived from operational records.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /inventory/export.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client reads or changes inventory, the Feedlot API shall return contract-defined stock, movement, projection, and export values and persist valid inventory changes in PostgreSQL.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and saved ration definitions exist, or the ration collection is empty.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response rations list contains saved ingredient, proportion, nutrition, cost, and approval fields.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /rations.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and submits a valid RationRequest for creation or revision.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 201 for creation or 200 for revision and the response ration contains the persisted definition and calculated contract fields, including costPerPound where declared.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends POST /rations or PATCH /rations/{rationId}.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and submits a valid ration optimization request with candidate mixes and nutrition requirements.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains the contract optimization result and cost comparison, including the lowest-cost qualifying candidate or qualifyingMixFound=false as applicable.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends POST /rations/optimization.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and the requested ration exists in a state eligible for approval.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains the rationId and updated approvalStatus, which is Approved where specified by the contract.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends POST /rations/{rationId}/approval.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client reads, creates, revises, optimizes, or approves a ration, the Feedlot API shall return contract-defined ration data and optimization or approval results and persist valid ration changes.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and saved feed plans exist, or the plan collection is empty.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response plans list contains saved plan details, execution state, and audit-related fields.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /feed-plans.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and submits a valid FeedPlanRequest with dated pen, ration, bunk rate, and animal-count values.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the response plan contains calculated planned quantity, quantity per animal, total feed cost, expected energy intake, and status fields.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends POST /feed-plans.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token, an existing plan, and a valid PlanReviewRequest or PlanStatusRequest.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response plan contains the saved reviewRequired value or requested execution status.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends POST /feed-plans/{planId}/review or PATCH /feed-plans/{planId}/status.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client reads, creates, reviews, or changes the execution status of a feed plan, the Feedlot API shall return and persist contract-defined pen-level plan details, calculated quantities, audit state, and status.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client records, corrects, or voids a feeding event, the Feedlot API shall persist the event and return its contract-defined variance, cost, energy, inventory movements, and updated lot feed totals.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-8\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and saved feeding events and lot allocations exist, or the event collection is empty.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /feeding-events.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response events list contains saved activity, lot allocations, and inventory movements.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.2\",\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and submits a valid FeedingEventRequest with planned and delivered quantities.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends POST /feeding-events.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 201 and the response contains the saved event, variance equal to deliveredQuantity minus plannedQuantity, calculated cost and energy, inventoryMovements, and updated lotFeedTotals.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.3\",\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token, an existing feeding event, known opening stock for its affected inventory items, and persisted receipts, adjustments, or other feeding events affecting those items, and either a valid correction request or an event eligible to be voided.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends PATCH /feeding-events/{eventId} or POST /feeding-events/{eventId}/void, then reads GET /inventory.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response event has the applicable Corrected or Voided status with corresponding reversal or correction movements and recalculated lotFeedTotals; the subsequent inventory response shows each affected item's stock reconciled from opening stock after applying all persisted receipts, adjustments, and non-voided feeding events, with a corrected event's movement replacing its original movement or a voided event's movement omitted rather than counted twice.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.4\",\n     \"given\": \"A client submits a feeding event that conflicts with current inventory or fails contract validation.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends POST /feeding-events.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is the contract-declared 409 or 422 and the response contains the contract ApiError fields.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.5\",\n     \"given\": \"A feeding event has been successfully saved and the App PostgreSQL database is available.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API process restarts and the client reads the event and inventory.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response contains the saved event and corresponding stock and lot totals.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client requests an operational, feed-to-gain, or profitability report or export, the Feedlot API shall return contract-defined permission-filtered rows, calculations, summaries, and requested export artifacts.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-7\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and operational feeding, performance, and inventory data with supported filters.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /reports/operational or GET /reports/operational/export.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response rows and summary match the filters, or the response contains a CSV file derived only from the authorized filtered rows.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.2\",\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and supplies a required date range plus optional breed, sex, or pen filters.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /reports/feed-to-gain.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response rows contain contract-defined ADG, feed, FCR, cost-of-gain, and energy fields for matching lots.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.3\",\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and supplies a valid feed-to-gain date range, supported filters, and format csv or pdf.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /reports/feed-to-gain/export.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response file artifact has contentType and content corresponding to the requested format and filtered authorized rows.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.4\",\n     \"given\": \"A client omits a required feed-to-gain date or supplies an export format outside the contract enum.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends a feed-to-gain report or export request.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 422 and the response error code is VALIDATION_ERROR.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.5\",\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and supplies supported profitability horizon, breed, penId, or roiStatus filters.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /reports/profitability or GET /reports/profitability/export.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response contains authorized matching profitability rows and canViewProfitability where declared, or a CSV file with those filtered authorized rows.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.6\",\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token with access to lot-report rows but without profitability.view or profitability.export, and matching profitability data exists.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /reports/profitability and GET /reports/profitability/export using supported filters.\",\n     \"then\": \"The report response status is 200, its canViewProfitability value is false, and its rows contain no non-null returnedInvestment, totalGainValue, netReturn, or roiPercent values; the export response status is 403 and contains no file artifact.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.7\",\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token with profitability.view but without profitability.export, and matching profitability data exists.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /reports/profitability and GET /reports/profitability/export using supported filters.\",\n     \"then\": \"The report response status is 200, its canViewProfitability value is true, and its matching rows contain the contract-defined profitability values; the export response status is 403 and contains no file artifact.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.8\",\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token with profitability.export but without profitability.view, and matching profitability data exists.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /reports/profitability and GET /reports/profitability/export using supported filters.\",\n     \"then\": \"The report response status is 200, its canViewProfitability value is false, and its rows contain no non-null returnedInvestment, totalGainValue, netReturn, or roiPercent values; the export response status is 200 and the response contains the contract-defined CSV file artifact.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and sample records may be absent, not yet loaded, or already loaded.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the response loaded, recordCount, records, and load status distinguish an empty set, a successful load, and already_loaded without duplicating records.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends GET /sample-data or POST /sample-data/load.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A client has a valid bearer token and sample records exist; the client records the GET /sample-data response records and recordCount before attempting reset or replacement.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The unconfirmed response status is the contract-declared 422 or 409, and the subsequent GET response records and recordCount are unchanged from before that request; the confirmed response has the completed operation status and resulting recordCount.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client sends POST /sample-data/reset or POST /sample-data/replace first without required confirmation, reads GET /sample-data, and then repeats the operation with explicit confirmation.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an authorized client reads, loads, resets, or replaces sample records, the Feedlot API shall return contract-defined sample status and records, avoid duplicate loading, and require explicit confirmation for reset or replacement.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 0.6666666666666666\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API is configured with an App PostgreSQL connection and a client successfully creates or updates a contract resource.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response contains the saved value and the returned record has the same id and field values as the successful write response.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API process restarts and the client retrieves the resource through its contract-defined read operation.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API is configured with a connection string named App and a successful contract write has completed.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"A row with the values written by the request is present in the App database.\",\n     \"when\": \"A test queries the configured PostgreSQL database for the affected entity.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An existing App PostgreSQL database contains data and lacks one or more tables required by the contract domain schema.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The pre-existing row values are unchanged and PostgreSQL contains the tables required by the contract operations.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API starts and upgrades the database schema.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 9,\n     \"lineStart\": 8,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"builder.Services.AddDbContext<AppDb>(o => o.UseNpgsql(builder.Configuration.GetConnectionString(\\\"App\\\")\\n    ?? throw new InvalidOperationException(\\\"No database connection is configured. Set ConnectionStrings__App (for example Host=...;Port=5432;Database=...;Username=...;Password=«SECRET_2»\")));\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 22,\n     \"lineStart\": 20,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"        using var scope = app.Services.CreateScope();\\n        var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<AppDb>();\\n        db.Database.EnsureCreated();\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 7,\n     \"lineStart\": 5,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/AppDb.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"public class AppDb(DbContextOptions<AppDb> options) : DbContext(options)\\n{\\n}\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot API shall store contract domain data in PostgreSQL using the configured connection string named App, preserve successful writes across API process restarts, and upgrade an existing App database to the contract domain schema without losing existing data.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"Q-4\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A fresh, empty App PostgreSQL database has Seed:Demo true.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"A database query reads 3 to 5 believable sample rows derived from corresponding contract examples in each application table, and each corresponding API collection response contains a nonempty list.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API starts successfully.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A contract-backed application table already contains operational rows and Seed:Demo is true.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The pre-existing row values are unchanged and no seed rows are added to that nonempty table.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API starts and runs SeedData.Run.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Seed:Demo is true and PostgreSQL rejects a seed write during startup.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Startup fails and the surfaced error identifies the seed-write failure without reporting successful readiness.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API starts.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 9,\n     \"lineStart\": 7,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/SeedData.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"    public static void Run(AppDb db)\\n    {\\n    }\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 24,\n     \"lineStart\": 23,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"        // sample rows, only when asked for (Seed__Demo=true): tests and the factory's own checks start on an empty database\\n        if (app.Configuration.GetValue<bool>(\\\"Seed:Demo\\\")) SeedData.Run(db);\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 170,\n     \"lineStart\": 169,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"                  - id: 701\\n                    vendor: \\\"Prairie Livestock\\\"\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When Seed:Demo is true, the Feedlot API shall use SeedData.Run at startup to insert 3 to 5 believable, contract-example-derived sample rows per application table when that table is empty, leave nonempty tables unchanged, and fail startup while surfacing any seed-write error.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-3\",\n    \"ASM-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An isolated App PostgreSQL database has no records and Seed:Demo is false.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Each response status is 200 and each response collection field is an empty list rather than an error or an assumed demo record.\",\n     \"when\": \"An authorized client calls contract collection endpoints, including GET /lots, GET /inventory, GET /rations, GET /feed-plans, and GET /feeding-events.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Seed:Demo is false and a test creates its own records through contract write operations.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response list contains the test-created records without depending on demo-seed record ids, counts, or values.\",\n     \"when\": \"The test reads the corresponding contract list operation.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When Seed:Demo is false, the Feedlot API shall serve contract collection operations based only on persisted records, including empty collections when no records exist.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-4\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n   \"metric\": \"100% of successfully acknowledged writes remain readable with the same persisted values after a process restart against the same App PostgreSQL database.\",\n   \"text\": \"Successful API writes to contract domain data use PostgreSQL durability and remain available after an API process restart.\"\n  }\n ],\n \"outOfScope\": [\n  \"Feedlot product screens and web-app UI implementation, which belong to the separate web-app repository.\",\n  \"Undocumented API paths and methods.\",\n  \"Additional authentication or role rules not explicitly declared by contracts/openapi.yaml.\"\n ],\n \"assumptions\": [\n  \"Interpret “a few” seed rows as 2 to 5 rows per application table; each row is based on an example for the corresponding entity in contracts/openapi.yaml.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nReview the spec."}